{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"PyTorch’s ROCm sum uses a hardware-specific multi-lane reduction order; neither Triton’s tree nor a sequential loop meets the very tight 99% elementwise requirement. I’m switching to a correctness-safe hybrid: one Triton pass emits both input gradients and the four already-rounded products, then PyTorch performs only the four order-sensitive reductions and two final adds. This still removes most eager launches and all rotate/cat traffic."}}
